// The same policy with `/8` written as `/9` -- a prefix-length slip, which is what range bugs in
// firewall rules actually look like.
//
// It still blocks 10.0.0.0 through 10.127.255.255, so a spot check on 10.1.2.3 looks fine. The
// whole upper half of the range -- 10.128.0.0 onward -- is no longer blocked.
//
// Every built-in check passes it: both rules fire, neither is redundant, nothing is dead. Only the
// property notices, and it names an address that gets through.

forbid (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Connect",
    resource
)
when { context.input.src.isInRange(ip("10.0.0.0/9")) };

permit ( principal, action == Anchor::Action::"Connect", resource );
